  "worked_solution": "The angles that the ray makes with the positive $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{5}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since the ray lies in the first quadrant, its polar equation is\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{5}{4}).\n$$",
